Error [jet.NonCAbiType]: `#Export(c)` `halve` declares the carrier `Int Err!`, which is not a C-compatible return.
  --> tests/ui/cffi_e3203_export_declared_failure.jet:1:12
    |
  1 | #Export(c) halve: fn(value: Int) -> Int Err! {
    |            ^^^^^
 Why: `#Import` / `#Export` functions must use types with a stable C ABI at the edge, and a C export is infallible: it returns no failure carrier.
 Fix: Handle every failure inside `halve` and declare it `Never!`.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E3203
